From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:37:29 -0400
Subject: fix: Peek review fixes (patch 0088)

The review of patch 0088 found these gaps, and this commit fixes each one:
- P14: drop the same-link dismissal. It swallowed a deliberate re-click,
  and also a click on the same link right after Escape. An activation of
  the source window in the peek's first 750 ms now brings the peek back to
  the front. A peek that is already closing is never raised.
- P17: peek windows are made with omit_from_session_restore. A restore no
  longer brings a peek back in the shared jar.
- P7: Open as Tab from a shared essential files the page in the Space on
  screen. A peek from a Space pin shows the pin's Space again before the
  page arrives.
- P9: Open in Split View pairs only with the pin it came from. It
  activates the pin first and never pairs with whatever tab is active. The
  page menu and the Mac File menu now leave out the split row over a peek
  that cannot split (LittleWindowOffersSplit), and the File menu's Cmd-O
  row reads Open as Tab.
- P16: path steps are matched without case. /auth counts only as the
  first step.
- P8: a target=_blank link from a pin in a Space with its own session
  loads in the peek. Navigate's contents contract is kept.
- Tests added for P7, P8 (Cmd-click), P10 off, P11 gesture, P12 exact
  margins, P14 grace and Escape, P16 host-only, and P17.

Why: the review found clicks that were lost, peeks restored in the wrong jar, pages filed in hidden Spaces, splits paired with an unrelated tab, and a blank peek in Spaces that have their own session.
Removable when: never; these are fixes to shipped Peek behaviour.
